# Environment Variables

Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in values.

```env
# App
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
AUTH_SECRET=generate-with-openssl-rand-base64-32
AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Neon PostgreSQL
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host/neondb?sslmode=require

# Firebase client (display real-time reads)
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# Firebase Admin (server queue writes)
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL=
FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Email (magic link + password reset)
RESEND_API_KEY=
EMAIL_FROM=LiveQue <onboarding@liveque.com>

# Stripe
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
STRIPE_PRICE_STARTER=
STRIPE_PRICE_PROFESSIONAL=

# Optional rate limiting
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# Legacy MKEHD migration (dev only — remove before production cutover)
LEGACY_TENANT_SLUG=mkehd
SKIP_QUEUE_AUTH=true
USE_LEGACY_QUEUE=false

# Seed scripts
SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL=
MKE_STAFF_EMAILS=
```

## Notes

- Keep your **existing Firebase project** for MKEHD — no new project required.
- `SKIP_QUEUE_AUTH=true` lets `/admin` work before staff accounts exist.
- After staff sign up, set `MKE_STAFF_EMAILS=you@example.com` and run `npm run db:seed`.
- Turn off `SKIP_QUEUE_AUTH` once MKE staff have memberships.
